The table structure information is (table names): 
['player', 'team', 'match', 'player_match', 'ball_by_ball', 'batsman_scored', 'wicket_taken', 'extra_runs']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
player.player_id / player.player_name: map every bowler id to the human‑readable name  
ball_by_ball.bowler: the bowler who delivered a particular ball  
batsman_scored.runs_scored: runs off the bat that are charged to the bowler  
extra_runs.extra_type / extra_runs.extra_runs: extra runs; wides & no‑balls count against the bowler, byes & leg‑byes do not  
wicket_taken.match_id / over_id / ball_id / kind_out: identify every dismissal and its type  
ball_by_ball.match_id / over_id / ball_id: allows us to attach the bowler to each dismissal or delivery  
Conditions that will probably be required  
• Join ball_by_ball ↔ batsman_scored ↔ extra_runs on (match_id, over_id, ball_id, innings_no)  
• Join wicket_taken ↔ ball_by_ball on the same composite key to know which bowler got each wicket  
• When counting wickets, ignore kind_out = 'run out' (and other non‑bowler dismissals if present)  
• Bowling average = (total runs conceded) / (total wickets taken) ; bowler with the minimum value is the answer  

Below are ten exploratory SELECT statements (each limited to 20 rows) that move from simple inspection to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1. List a few distinct bowler IDs that occur in ball_by_ball
SELECT DISTINCT "bowler"
FROM "ball_by_ball"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Attach bowler IDs to names for easy reading
SELECT DISTINCT bb."bowler", p."player_name"
FROM "ball_by_ball" AS bb
JOIN "player"       AS p ON p."player_id" = bb."bowler"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Look at how many balls each bowler has delivered
SELECT bb."bowler", p."player_name", COUNT(*) AS "balls_bowled"
FROM "ball_by_ball" AS bb
JOIN "player"       AS p ON p."player_id" = bb."bowler"
GROUP BY bb."bowler"
ORDER BY "balls_bowled" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Sum of runs off the bat conceded by every bowler
SELECT bb."bowler", SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "bat_runs"
FROM "ball_by_ball" AS bb
JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
  ON bs."match_id" = bb."match_id"
 AND bs."over_id"  = bb."over_id"
 AND bs."ball_id"  = bb."ball_id"
 AND bs."innings_no" = bb."innings_no"
GROUP BY bb."bowler"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Extra runs that are charged to the bowler (wides & no‑balls only)
SELECT bb."bowler",
       SUM(er."extra_runs") AS "bowler_extras"
FROM "ball_by_ball" AS bb
JOIN "extra_runs"   AS er
  ON er."match_id" = bb."match_id"
 AND er."over_id"  = bb."over_id"
 AND er."ball_id"  = bb."ball_id"
 AND er."innings_no" = bb."innings_no"
WHERE er."extra_type" IN ('wides', 'noballs')
GROUP BY bb."bowler"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Combine the two previous queries to get total runs conceded
SELECT r1."bowler",
       COALESCE(r1."bat_runs",0) + COALESCE(r2."bowler_extras",0) AS "total_runs_conceded"
FROM (
    SELECT bb."bowler", SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "bat_runs"
    FROM "ball_by_ball" AS bb
    JOIN "batsman_scored" AS bs
      ON bs."match_id" = bb."match_id"
     AND bs."over_id"  = bb."over_id"
     AND bs."ball_id"  = bb."ball_id"
     AND bs."innings_no" = bb."innings_no"
    GROUP BY bb."bowler"
) AS r1
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT bb."bowler", SUM(er."extra_runs") AS "bowler_extras"
    FROM "ball_by_ball" AS bb
    JOIN "extra_runs"   AS er
      ON er."match_id" = bb."match_id"
     AND er."over_id"  = bb."over_id"
     AND er."ball_id"  = bb."ball_id"
     AND er."innings_no" = bb."innings_no"
    WHERE er."extra_type" IN ('wides', 'noballs')
    GROUP BY bb."bowler"
) AS r2
ON r1."bowler" = r2."bowler"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Count every dismissal that is credited to the bowler
SELECT bb."bowler", COUNT(*) AS "wickets"
FROM "wicket_taken" AS wt
JOIN "ball_by_ball" AS bb
  ON wt."match_id" = bb."match_id"
 AND wt."over_id"  = bb."over_id"
 AND wt."ball_id"  = bb."ball_id"
 AND wt."innings_no" = bb."innings_no"
WHERE wt."kind_out" NOT IN ('run out')  -- add more if necessary
GROUP BY bb."bowler"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
